From 95e0210feef1e46b4bf6951e3e45969b3d36c84d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stevostar1234 <skybasteven@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 20:25:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Second-opinion follow-up for the intake, top-up and dispatch
 guards

- tests/forms.test.js asserted the old first-purchase expression, so the
  normal local suite failed on this branch; it now asserts the durable
  evidence rule and the held-for-repair branch instead.
- The cleared-quantity rejection no longer tells staff to "reprocess" the
  submission: no such action exists and the owner chose manual correction
  or one fresh form (14 September audit). A negative count typed by hand
  is treated like a blank one.
- Retry on a genuinely Sent dispatch returns the accepted-email guidance
  instead of pointing at a blank Send Error.
- A hand-queued dispatch with an acceptance timestamp is restored to Sent
  rather than Skipped, so the panel's last-sent date and the Status-based
  duplicate guards still see it.
- New test with a preparation reminder, a kind the previous code really did
  resend after a relabel; the colleague test user now uses the runner's
  profile like NTEUpdateIssuesPanelTest instead of the org's oldest user.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
